<article class="env-lemma" id="0A7Y">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A7Y">Lemma <span data-tag="0A7Y">47.17.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring and let $\omega _ A^\bullet $ be a dualizing complex. Let $A \to B$ be a surjective ring map and let $\omega _ B^\bullet = R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (B, \omega _ A^\bullet )$ be the dualizing complex for $B$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/0A7I" data-tag="0A7I">47.15.9</a>. Then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \delta _{\omega _ B^\bullet } = \delta _{\omega _ A^\bullet }|_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)}  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the definition of the functions and Lemma <a href="/tag/0A7N" data-tag="0A7N">47.16.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>